      "budget_share": 0.5,
      "why": "Full pipelining gives 1 result/cycle, so throughput = Fmax. To hit >=1 MSPS we need Fmax >= 1 MHz, which is trivially met; the real constraint is area. N+2 latency is fine for a control loop. I focus on the low-end of the accuracy/area trade-off: data_width 12-16 and n_iter 10-16 should bracket the max_abs_err <= 2^-10 boundary. angle_guard and frac_guard are kept small to minimise area while still allowing the optimizer to find the minimal guard that meets the error spec. This family has the most registers (one per stage), so it will likely be area-heavy, but it is the baseline for the 1-result/cycle requirement."
    },
    {
      "family": "pipelined_m",
      "ranges": [
        {
          "param": "data_width",
          "low": 12,
          "high": 16
        ,
